 "about": "Beech forest with silver fir, sycamore, Italian maple and whitebeam from about 900 to 1800 m; Turkey and downy oak, hop hornbeam, manna ash and sweet chestnut below it; black pine plantings on the slopes and Norway spruce plantings in the north; mountain pine on the Maiella, dwarf juniper above the trees, and common juniper, hawthorn, hazel and broom on the pastures; rush-leaved moor-grass on the limestone slopes, mat-grass and bilberry on the sandstone ridge, alpine flowers, ferns and bracken; large sheep flocks, white Marchigiana cattle, free-ranging horses, goats, and Apennine chamois on the high rock; stone villages with low terracotta roofs.",
